  "narration": {
    "title": "The Rookie Class Sends Its Report Card",
    "intro": "Today belongs to the newcomers. Munetaka Murakami leads a rookie hitting board that runs deep, and a pair of young arms are keeping their ERAs where veterans would be jealous. Here's who's arrived and who's climbing.",
    "rookies_lead": "Munetaka Murakami tops the rookie bats with a .938 OPS and 20 home runs for the White Sox, already the class of this group. Colorado has two on the list, with Cole Carrigg at .907 and TJ Rumfield at .859, while Atlanta's Didier Fuentes (2.41 ERA) and San Diego's Bradgley Rodriguez (2.00) lead the rookie arms.",
